+## Trusted reverse proxy login
+
+To use authentication supplied by a reverse proxy, set the proxy's **connection IP** in `ReverseProxyWhitelist` and the username header in `ReverseProxyUserHeader`:
+
+```toml
+ReverseProxyWhitelist = "192.0.2.0/24, 2001:db8::/32"
+ReverseProxyUserHeader = "Remote-User"
+```
+
+`Remote-User` is the default header. A trusted request creates its user on first login; the first user becomes an administrator. `ReverseProxyDefaultUser` optionally supplies a username when the trusted proxy sends no username header. Use `@` in the whitelist for a Unix socket connection. An empty whitelist disables proxy login. Only include addresses that can reach Navidrome through a proxy that sets or clears the username header; forwarded IP headers do not grant trust.
+
 ## Documentation
 All documentation can be found in the project's website: https://www.navidrome.org/docs. 
